  "note": "assessBillOfSale(d) returns { classification, missingItemCount, riskFlagCount, missingItems } and no flags, so this is a SPLIT engine: the oracle pins detectFlaggedIssues(state) as expected.flaggedIssues with flagsArgs [\"state\"], mirroring form-app.js (the grader result is not passed to the detector). Classification is first-match: any risk condition (finance outstanding, seller not registered keeper, V5C missing, V5C mismatch, description mismatch) -> 'risk-flagged'; any missing required item -> 'incomplete'; else 'complete'. Flags are stable-sorted high > medium > low. The MOT flag uses the sale year (not the wall clock) when a sale date is present. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas united-kingdom-vehicle-bill-of-sale --update",
